**Overall: 7/10 → 9/10**

### The five real fixes

1. **H2 3's heading was unfulfilled.** It's titled *"Why Simone Biles asked her coach 'Did I do it?'"* and the section never mentioned it — the second pass trimmed the restatements out and left the heading writing a cheque the section no longer cashed. The safe-space-to-fail paragraph now closes on why Boorman was the person she asked.
2. **H2 3 → H2 4 was a five-year jump with no bridge.** Added one line carrying "silent cries" into Tokyo. It avoids the word *weakness* in house voice, since the piece argues the opposite.
3. **H2 5 → H2 6 was the worst seam** — a backward jump from post-Tokyo aftermath to January 2018 with no signal. New opener: *"She was in that stadium for a reason, and it starts three years earlier."*
4. **"Which brings us to the half-point" was a false transition** — a connective claiming a link the Owens beat doesn't make. Replaced with a bridge that carries the H2 2 hallway language ("put her own body in the room") and the love-blanky beat into Landi standing on the mat. That stitch was the biggest available win: it ties three scenes across the whole piece.
5. **"the twisties" was used before the body defined it** (only the FAQ did). First use now carries Boorman's cold-open phrasing.

Plus: H2 9's paragraph order swapped so the section opens on the 50-50 that H2 8 sets up, rather than an NFL roster note — which also puts April/June/August back in chronological order.

### The constraint
The file was at 4,499 words against a hard 4,500 lint ceiling, so every bridge was paid for by a cut. All cuts were paraphrase-after-quote redundancy (the Rio paragraph said *nineteen/summit* three times; "She did not fire them" and "She left the gym repeatedly" each restated the line beside them). Net **4,499 → 4,492**, so the pass returned 7 words of headroom rather than spending it. Lint: **0 fail** (the one warn is the pre-existing verbatim Biles quote already documented in the ledger).

### Preserved
Frontmatter, FAQs, all ledgers, all internal links, and everything fresh-eyes flagged as untouchable — the cold open, the hallway scene, the Tokyo timeline form, the Kirk/Morgan concession, the spotter, and the close.

### One thing left for you
`"Owens is in Indianapolis now, ninth NFL season."` is still a one-clause orphan in H2 9 — nothing picks it up. I left it because the FORMULA FINGERPRINT LEDGER names Owens-with-the-Colts as part of the current-tense anchor set, but it's the cheapest 8 words on the page if the next refresh needs room.
